@startuml
'==== Title ====
title "As a Buyer, I want to use the Web UI to bid on an auction." - SD %n()

'==== basic style ====
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam objectFontSize 20
skinparam backgroundColor CornSilk
skinparam objectBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFE0
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3B4953
skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor black
hidefootbox
autonumber

' ==== Actor and participants ====
actor Buyer
participant ":Frontend" as FE
participant ":Backend" as BE
participant ":db" as db

note over FE
This diagram assumes that a list of auctions is
displayed and that, for each individual auction,
there are buttons for the possible actions on
that auction, including **creating a bid**.

To view how the Buyer has this OPTION to
create a bid, please see [[pre-condition-diagram/OPTIONS_Before_POST.puml this diagram]]
end note





Buyer -> FE : I want to place a bid on %n()an auction with a value of x.
activate FE

note over FE
Currency is predetermined
by the currency of the auction
end note

FE -> BE : POST {bids href} + %n(){placeBidRequestDTO}
activate BE

ref over BE
[[/rest-sd-ref-diagrams/POST_Place_Bid_SD.puml POST bid on /auctions/{auctionId}/bids]]
end ref

BE --> FE : 201 Created + bidResponseDTO %n() + auction link + bids link
deactivate BE
FE --> Buyer : Bid successfully %n()placed on auction.
deactivate FE

@enduml